# Octo generated Terraform / Terragrunt artifacts.
# `.octo/` and `.octo-tf/` are NOT ignored - model state, resource state, terraform state, and the
# generated Terraform belong in the repo, so a change to them shows up in review. What apply leaves
# behind does not. The `terraform.tfstate` in a module folder is one of those leftovers: octo checks
# it out of `.octo/` before every terraform command and back in after, so the copy under `.octo/` is
# the one that is kept.
.terragrunt-cache/
*.tfstate*
!.octo/*.tfstate
.octo/local-state.lock
# The journal: files per command, archived per lock, which would land in every pull request.
.octo/journal.*
.octo/archives/

